I've been experimenting a bit with the ki-rin after reading some posts 
by Todd Pytel. ( news:<20050621162211.40c9045f.tppytel@nospam.org> )

Even though I like this powerful pet candidate I must say that it seems 
rather buggy that Nethack considers it to have hands and feet. All the 
Ki-rin I've seen pictured has been mostly horse-like with four hooved 
legs. It feels a bit strange to imagine this creature wearing gloves and 
boots, wielding a shield, and even opening doors. Wearing a helm isn't 
much better, though perhaps I can accept the amulet-wearing.

The Nethack description says:
"The ki-rin is a strange-looking flying creature. It has scales, a mane 
like a lion, a tail, hooves, and a horn. It is brightly colored, and can 
usually be found flying in the sky looking for good deeds to reward."

Google images link:
http://images.google.com/images?q=ki-rin&hl=en&lr=&c2coff=1
&safe=off&sa=N&tab=wi

I was experimenting and trying to create a really powerful flying steed 
pet. What would you equip your Ki-rin with (accepting its current 
powerful status)? Cornuthaum sounds like a really good idea, but does 
the magic cancellation effect really work for a pet? Which 'magical 
properties of worn or put on equipment' matters for a pet? I think speed 
boots would probably be a waste. Reflection seems to work fine though, 
both from the amulet and the shield. Would it wear Will a leveled-up Ki-
rin (non-pet) ever cast Touch of Death? Do pets ever use offensive 
magic? Which defensive/miscellanous/offensive items does a pet use 
(since it seems to not be the same as a hostile creature)?

